---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const topologyDiagram = ` Any device on the Headscale mesh
    |
    | Direct HTTP, one port per service (WireGuard encrypted, no reverse proxy)
    v
[ Pi 4B — autobot — 100.64.0.1 ]
    |
    +-- Vaultwarden      :8081
    +-- Gitea + CI       :8087 / :8088
    +-- Headscale        :8086  (mesh control plane — every device registers here)
    +-- Pi-hole          :8053  (+ DNS on :53)
    +-- Samba            :445   (centralized storage)
    +-- Syncthing        :22000 (multi-device sync)
    +-- Uptime Kuma       :8082  (real status source)
    +-- Netdata          :19999
    +-- Portfolio (this site) :8090

  Built, version-controlled, not currently running:
    Nextcloud + MariaDB + Redis, Home Assistant

  Retired entirely (git history only, see ADR-009):
    Traefik, Portainer, CrowdSec, the full Windows
    observability/secrets/auth stack (11 containers)
`;
---

<Base title="Architecture">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4 text-brand-light">Architecture</h1>
  <p class="text-lg text-text-muted mb-12 max-w-2xl">
    Single node, direct mesh access. No reverse proxy, no second node in daily use —
    every service is reachable at its own mesh-IP:port over Headscale. That's a deliberate
    simplification, not an oversight — see the design decisions below.
  </p>

  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 text-brand">Network Topology</h2>
    <div class="border border-surface-light rounded-lg p-8 bg-surface-light/20 overflow-x-auto">
      <pre class="text-sm text-text-muted font-mono leading-relaxed">{topologyDiagram}</pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 text-brand">Traffic Flow</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 text-text-muted">
      <li>User (or another mesh device) hits <code class="text-brand-light bg-surface-light px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">http://100.64.0.1:PORT</code> directly</li>
      <li>Headscale-assigned mesh IP routes the connection over WireGuard — encrypted end to end</li>
      <li>Docker maps that port straight to the container, no routing layer in between</li>
      <li>Nothing is reachable outside the mesh — access control is mesh membership itself, not an auth layer in front</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 text-brand">Stack Overview</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border border-surface-light rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        <thead class="bg-surface-light/50">
          <tr>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-brand-light">Stack</th>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-brand-light">Services</th>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-brand-light">Purpose</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-surface-light">
          <tr class="hover:bg-surface-light/20"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">headscale</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">headscale</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">Self-hosted mesh control plane</td></tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-surface-light/20"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">gitops</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">gitea, act-runner (systemd)</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">Self-hosted Git + CI/CD</td></tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-surface-light/20"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">apps</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">vaultwarden (nextcloud/mariadb/redis kept, not running)</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">Passwords</td></tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-surface-light/20"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">nas</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">samba, syncthing</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">Centralized storage + multi-device sync</td></tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-surface-light/20"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">network</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">pihole, pihole-exporter</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">DNS ad-blocking + metrics</td></tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-surface-light/20"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">monitoring</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">netdata</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">Real-time system + container metrics (single container, replaced a 6-container stack)</td></tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-surface-light/20"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">uptime-kuma</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">uptime-kuma</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">Real up/down status — the actual source of truth</td></tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-surface-light/20"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">portfolio</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">astro site (this one)</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">Project showcase</td></tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-surface-light/20"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">smarthome</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">homeassistant</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-text-muted">Home automation — built, not currently running</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 text-brand">Phase Plan</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="border-l-4 border-green-500 pl-4">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-green-400">Phase 1 — Pi Core</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Docker Compose only. K3s, ArgoCD, and Helmfile evaluated and removed — too much RAM overhead for a 4GB box.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-4 border-green-500 pl-4">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-green-400">Phase 2 — Windows Offload</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Full observability + secrets + auth stack (Grafana, Prometheus, Loki, Tempo, Alertmanager, Authelia, Infisical) moved to a second node to keep the Pi under budget.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-4 border-green-500 pl-4">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-green-400">Phase 3 — Self-Hosted Control Plane</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Headscale replaces Tailscale SaaS after a coordination-server outage locked out the password vault.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-4 border-green-500 pl-4">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-green-400">Phase 4 — GitOps</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Gitea + act_runner for real push-to-deploy, replacing manual bundle+SCP workflow.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-light pl-4">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-light">Phase 5 — The Retirement (current)</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">
          The Phase 2 stack (11 containers), plus Traefik, Portainer, and CrowdSec, retired per ADR-009 —
          single-operator homelab, the complexity wasn't earning its RAM. Netdata replaces the six-container
          metrics stack. Down to a lean core that actually gets used daily.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 text-brand">Key Design Decisions</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-text-muted">
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-brand-light font-bold shrink-0">No K3s</span><span>Control plane alone costs 600&ndash;800MB idle RAM — too much before a single real workload runs</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-brand-light font-bold shrink-0">No reverse proxy</span><span>Traefik retired — direct mesh-IP:port per service is simpler at this scale and one less thing that can break access to everything at once</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-brand-light font-bold shrink-0">No auth layer</span><span>Authelia retired — mesh membership is the access boundary; no multi-user need to justify SSO/2FA infrastructure</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-brand-light font-bold shrink-0">No full observability stack</span><span>Prometheus/Grafana/Loki/Tempo/Alertmanager retired — Uptime Kuma + Netdata cover what actually gets checked</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-brand-light font-bold shrink-0">No TLS needed</span><span>WireGuard (Headscale mesh) encrypts all traffic end to end — TLS termination would be redundant inside the mesh</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-brand-light font-bold shrink-0">Retire, don't delete</span><span>Everything decommissioned moves through a <code>_retired/</code> folder before removal — recoverable via git history, nothing silently gone</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
